{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>“Speak to Moses and to Aaron, saying: Speak to the children of Israel”</b> — The commandments in these parashiyyot (Leviticus 11:1–47) apply both to Israel and to the priests, but their subject matter pertains preeminently to the priests. For they must constantly guard against contact with impurity, because they need to enter the Sanctuary and eat of the holy offerings. Moreover, if Israelites inadvertently transgress in these matters, they are obligated to bring a sacrifice that the priests offer. Furthermore, He commanded them “and to distinguish between the sacred and the profane, and between the impure and the pure” (Leviticus 10:10). So they must instruct Israel concerning the impure and the pure, so that they may be cautious in them. Therefore this divine address was to Moses and to Aaron both, or to Moses that he should speak to Aaron, and He commanded them both: “Speak to the children of Israel.” It is for this reason that these were stated in the Book of the Law of the Priests (i.e., Leviticus). And in the parashah He gave warning concerning eating and concerning impurity — that they not defile the Tabernacle and its holy things."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:52:24.327459716Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}